ed media is\u00a0generally considered\u00a0the most trustworthy because it comes from independent sources like customers, journalists, and influencers, rather than the brand itself.","inLanguage":"en-US"},"inLanguage":"en-US"},{"@type":"Question","@id":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/poem-framework-in-digital-marketing\/#faq-question-1781941214459","position":5,"url":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/poem-framework-in-digital-marketing\/#faq-question-1781941214459","name":"Q5. Can small businesses use the POEM framework?","answerCount":1,"acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Absolutely. Even with a small budget, a business can build owned media (blog\u00a0and\u00a0website), invest modestly in paid ads, and focus on getting reviews and word-of-mouth. The framework scales to any size.","inLanguage":"en-US"},"inLanguage":"en-US"},{"@type":"Question","@id":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/poem-framework-in-digital-marketing\/#faq-question-1781941228803","position":6,"url":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/poem-framework-in-digital-marketing\/#faq-question-1781941228803","name":"Q6. What is the difference between owned and earned media?","answerCount":1,"acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Owned media is what you create and control directly (your website, blog, emails). Earned media is what others say about you (reviews, press, social shares) that you did not pay for directly.","inLanguage":"en-US"},"inLanguage":"en-US"},{"@type":"Question","@id":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/poem-framework-in-digital-marketing\/#faq-question-1781941241541","position":7,"url":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/poem-framework-in-digital-marketing\/#faq-question-1781941241541","name":"Q7. How does the POEM framework help with SEO?","answerCount":1,"acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The POEM framework strengthens SEO through owned media (website and blog content), earned media (backlinks and brand mentions), and paid media that drives\u00a0additional\u00a0visibility. Together, they help improve search rankings and organic traffic over time.","inLanguage":"en-US"},"inLanguage":"en-US"},{"@type":"Question","@id":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/poem-framework-in-digital-marketing\/#faq-question-1781941255213","position":8,"url":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/poem-framework-in-digital-marketing\/#faq-question-1781941255213","name":"Q8. Is influencer marketing paid media or earned media?","answerCount":1,"acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"It can be both. Sponsored influencer collaborations are paid media, while organic mentions from influencers without compensation are earned media. Many brands use paid partnerships to generate\u00a0additional\u00a0earned exposure.","inLanguage":"en-US"},"inLanguage":"en-US"},{"@type":"Question","@id":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/poem-framework-in-digital-marketing\/#faq-question-1781941270110","position":9,"url":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/poem-framework-in-digital-marketing\/#faq-question-1781941270110","name":"Q9. How often should I review my POEM strategy?","answerCount":1,"acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Review paid media weekly to track performance and adjust campaigns. Owned and earned media can typically be reviewed monthly to measure content, SEO, brand mentions, and overall results.","inLanguage":"en-US"},"inLanguage":"en-US"},{"@type":"Question","@id":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/poem-framework-in-digital-marketing\/#faq-question-1781941282407","position":10,"url":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/poem-framework-in-digital-marketing\/#faq-question-1781941282407","name":"Q10. What tools can I use to manage each part of the POEM model?","answerCount":1,"acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Popular tools include Google Ads and Meta Ads Manager for paid media, WordPress and Google Search Console for owned media, and Brand24 or Mention for tracking earned media and brand mentions.","inLanguage":"en-US"},"inLanguage":"en-US"},{"@type":"Question","@id":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/poem-framework-in-digital-marketing\/#faq-question-1781941323729","position":11,"url":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/poem-framework-in-digital-marketing\/#faq-question-1781941323729","name":"Q11. Can the POEM framework be used for offline marketing?","answerCount":1,"acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. The framework applies to both digital and traditional marketing. For example, TV ads are paid media, brochures are owned media, and newspaper coverage is earned media. The same principles work across all marketing channels.","inLanguage":"en-US"},"inLanguage":"en-US"}]}},"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/20130","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/post"}],"author":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/users\/15"}],"replies":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/comments?post=20130"}],"version-history":[{"count":4,"href":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/20130\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":20935,"href":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/20130\/revisions\/20935"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media\/20131"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=20130"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"category","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/categories?post=20130"},{"taxonomy":"post_tag","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/tags?post=20130"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}}